# Go Conventions

## Error Handling

- Return errors, never `log.Fatal`
- Wrap errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`
- Use sentinel errors from `services/errors.go` where appropriate

```go
// ❌ BAD
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}

// ✅ GOOD
if err != nil {
    return fmt.Errorf("failed to fetch config: %w", err)
}
```

## GitHub API Safety

Nil-check all GitHub API responses before dereferencing:

```go
// ❌ BAD
name := *repo.Name

// ✅ GOOD
if repo.Name != nil {
    name = *repo.Name
}
```

## Logging

Use `log/slog` for all logging—never `log` or `fmt.Print` for operational output:

```go
slog.Info("processing webhook", "delivery_id", deliveryID, "repo", repoName)
slog.Error("failed to fetch file", "error", err, "path", filePath)
```

## Testing

- Always run tests with `-race` flag: `go test -race ./...`
- Use `httpmock` for HTTP mocking (see `tests/utils.go` for patterns)
- Test files live alongside source: `foo.go` → `foo_test.go`

## Pointers

Use `github.Ptr()` (not deprecated `github.String`/`github.Int`/`github.Bool`):

```go
// ❌ BAD (deprecated)
req.Title = github.String("PR title")

// ✅ GOOD
req.Title = github.Ptr("PR title")
```
